{"availability":"available","full":"thesephist/kin","name":"kin","description":"A refined tool for exploring open-source projects on GitHub with a file tree, rich Markdown and image previews, multi-pane multi-tab layouts and first-class support for Ink syntax highlighting.","category":"Productivity","language":"JavaScript","stars":24,"forks":1,"created":"2021-06-11T19:58:39Z","updated":"2021-06-15T21:59:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://code.dotink.co","topics":["file-browser","github-api","ink-programming-language","torus-dom"],"demo":"https://code.dotink.co/demo","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.220Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.220Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.220Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.220Z","stars":24,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Ink codebase browser is a tool to explore open-source code on GitHub, especially my side projects written in the Ink programming language. It offers multi-pane, multi-tab interfaces for looking at source code from projects on GitHub, and generates Markdown previews and syntax highlighting for many languages including Ink.","The codebase browser is a full-stack Ink application. It's written in pure Ink except for the syntax highlighting library used to highlight non-Ink source code (highlight.js) and Torus used as the UI rendering backend. In addition to these libraries, the project leans on September for building the frontend and for syntax highlighting Ink source code; and it depends on Merlot for rendering Markdown file previews.","\"Kin\" was my codename for the project before I gave it its final name of the Ink codebase browser — I liked the name because it's an anagram of \"ink\", and it's short."],"features":["There are three main problems I wanted to solve with the codebase browser.","Most of my side projects written in Ink are open-source on GitHub, but GitHub doesn't (yet) syntax highlight Ink source code. This makes Ink code harder to read on GitHub than it has to be.","GitHub's file browser interface isn't great for just exploring the file hierarchy of a project. Compared to modern code editors, with a file tree sidebar, multi-pane and multi-tab layouts,","Frequently, I find myself needing to reference Ink source files on my GitHub from elsewhere on the Internet like a blog, and I'm disappointed that I can't simply link to a line-numbered, syntax-highlighted file preview.…","The codebase browser solves all of these problems through the main interface and the \"proxy\" service described below. In addition, to improve the experience of looking around a project the app supports some extra…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thesephist/kin/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f101ced2348dcd02c37c5ead63f8cbabb9cce8a69c29acb0a93564a8067bd3a6","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.393Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.393Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The Ink codebase browser is a tool to explore open-source code on GitHub, especially my side projects written in the Ink programming language. It offers multi-pane, multi-tab interfaces for looking at source code from projects on GitHub, and generates Markdown previews and syntax highlighting for many languages including Ink.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thesephist/kin/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"To run the server, you'll need to replace the dummy token in secrets.sample.ink with your GitHub access token and copy it to secrets.ink.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thesephist/kin/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f101ced2348dcd02c37c5ead63f8cbabb9cce8a69c29acb0a93564a8067bd3a6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thesephist/kin/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:02.394Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2021-06-15T21:59:40Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl